now that leads to one more topic that i  want to get to i was on wqam in miami  this morning with zach krantz joe rose  who's been hosting that show for years  and i've been on that show every friday  morning for years uh joe was off zach  and i were talking about  the rogers situation and he raised the  question of  how many teams would rogers make  into  super bowl contenders immediately if the  trade happened right now regardless of  who they currently have and obviously  there are a lot of teams that already  are super bowl contenders  without aaron rodgers or yes they're  they're already like the bills yeah the  bills are a super bowl contender with  josh allen if for some reason the bills  would decide to trade for aaron rodgers  which they would never do because they  have josh allen they're still a super  bowl contender so what i've done is i've  gone through team by team  and  i'm curious about the teams that  currently aren't in my mind based upon  their their present quarterback  situation true super bowl contenders  does rogers make them into contenders  yes or no  now  before i get to that here are the teams  that i think are contenders  with or without  aaron rodgers super bowl contenders with  or without rogers on the team  the bills the patriots and yes i believe  the patriots are super bowl contenders  given  the upgrades they've made this off  season and the presence  of bill belichick as the head coach  the steelers  the browns the ravens the titans the  colts  the  chiefs and the chargers in the afc those  are the teams that i think are super  bowl contenders with or without aaron  rodgers in the nfc  the cowboys  and even though i think washington's  going to win the division i think if it  works for the cowboys they're more  likely to be a super bowl contender if  that makes any sense so i'm going to say  the cowboys the only super bowl  contender out of the nfc east for now  even though i think washington wins the  division  the buccaneers the saints  the rams  the seahawks and the 49ers those are all  the teams that are super bowl contenders  if for some reason they would decide hey  let's go ahead and get aaron rodgers and  the packers will trade him now here are  the teams that become contenders  for the super bowl  who i currently think aren't  you put in aaron rodgers and they're  contenders  the dolphins become super bowl  contenders they currently aren't  the raiders become super bowl contenders  in my mind they currently aren't the  broncos become super bowl contenders in  my mind they currently aren't washington  becomes a super bowl contender in my  mind even though i think they're going  to win the division i don't think  they're going to have enough to punch  through to the super bowl  the vikings become super bowl contenders  in my mind they currently aren't the  bears  they're not going to do it but they  would become super bowl contenders in my  mind they currently aren't  and then the others i've added  the panthers  and the cardinals i don't think either  team is a super bowl contender right now  i think they would be with aaron rodgers  the teams i struggled with  were the falcons  and  the giants i put them on the nose side  and these are the teams that i think  aaron rodgers wouldn't make them into  super bowl contenders jets bengals  texans jaguars  giants eagles lions falcons  but the two on which i was the closest  are the giants and the falcons and it's  no coincidence that they're nfc teams  because the afc is so damn top heavy  i don't care who the quarterback is of  the jets this year they're not a super  bowl contender they're not ready yet  from a personnel standpoint the bengals  have a long way to go to be super bowl  contenders the texans have the worst  roster in the nfl right now and the  jaguars have a long way to go as well  not that the jaguars would want aaron  rodgers if the opportunity arose or the  bengals for that matter or the jets for  that matter again there aren't many  teams that would want him right now i  think the broncos are the clear leader  right now  the raiders as i said could get into it  and the other side of it too and i'm  glad i thought of this  rogers has to want to go  to the team that would trade for him  and some of you will say in response to  that but he doesn't have a no trade  clause well  for a starting quarterback  a no trade clause is meaningless  because  think about this if you're the general  manager of a team  and you are trading for a quarterback a  guy that you want to come in and set the  tone for the organization show up stay  late hold teammates accountable check  every box and then some be the face of  the team at least from the locker room  standpoint  if he doesn't want to be there  do you really want him  i think a key ingredient  to making it work especially at this  stage of the year is to have full buy-in  from the quarterback so hey the dolphins  become super bowl contenders with aaron  rodgers but if aaron rodgers doesn't  want to live and play in miami this year  if he doesn't want to be on the dolphins  this year you're not going to make that  trade  because he don't want to be there he may  not show up remember when richard  seymour was traded from the patriots to  the raiders and it took a few days for  him to recognize oh god i've been traded  from one of the best teams in the nfl  one of the worst at the time the raiders  were one of the worst  it took him a while to realize i just  better go now it's easier to do that  with a non-quarterback  a quarterback can say fine i'll show up  but don't expect me to do all the stuff  that a quarterback  who's all in would do and i think it's  one of the reasons why the bears didn't  go after carson wentz remember they were  linked to carson wentz wentz didn't want  to go there wence doesn't have no trade  clause it doesn't matter if wence  doesn't want to be in chicago the bears  aren't going to waste their time trading  for him so that's the other thing to  keep in mind if he gets traded this year  i think it's the broncos maybe the  raiders  after this year there will be more teams  at the table the question is which teams  would aaron rodgers be willing to play  for the problem is i mean think about it  the west coast teams that's where he  wants to go well the ramps have matthew  stafford and they gave up a lot to get  him  they're not going to give up on him  after one year the 49ers who the hell  knows what they're going to do because  they wanted aaron rodgers and they're so  desperate to atone for their failure to  draft patrick mahomes and their failure  to take tom brady up on his interest in  the team that maybe they would do  something crazy like throw everyone  overboard and go get aaron rodgers trey  lance for aaron rodgers straight up  maybe that would happen who knows  the raiders and the broncos i think  would still be the two teams to watch  next year but maybe the possibility of  having more teams at the table could  leverage one of those teams to give up  more and of course from roger's  perspective he doesn't want the team  he's going to to give up too much  because he's got to go play for that  team you don't want the team to be  gutted you don't want the team's draft  picks for the next several years to all  be gone  as part of the transaction that brought  you there  so  up  interesting dynamics to say the least  and we'll find out in a couple of weeks  whether he shows up but the bottom line  is i think if he shows up that gives him  a better chance to get out this year  instead of next year  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

